### Foundational thesis

CBBC v0.3 — Branching Execution & Parallelism Periodicity Architecture

A distributed autonomous computing architecture integrating Byzantine fault tolerance, behavioral policy authorization, self-binding, self-bootstrapping, branching execution, parallel computation, periodic synchronization, and persistent cryptographic integrity.

Its defining proposition is that computational autonomy should be achieved through bounded execution and independently verifiable evidence—not through unrestricted automation.

The specification below establishes CBBC v0.3 as a testable engineering design, integrating the existing v0.2 consensus foundation with Branching Execution, Parallel Processing, Periodicity, Self-Binding, Self-Bootstrapping, and the Palladium Persistent Storage Array.

One important boundary: CBBC's behavioral layer and autonomous execution extensions are proposed protocol designs, not independently proven Byzantine fault-tolerant algorithms. The specification therefore separates established BFT assumptions from new mechanisms that require implementation, formal verification, and security review.

