# 11. Self-Bootstrapping Engine

## 11.1 SBE lifecycle

SBE initializes a system through a controlled verification sequence.

```text
DISCOVER
   |
AUTHENTICATE
   |
VERIFY ENVIRONMENT
   |
LOAD APPROVED POLICY
   |
VERIFY VALIDATOR MEMBERSHIP
   |
PROVISION ISOLATED RESOURCES
   |
VERIFY RESOURCE ATTESTATIONS
   |
INITIALIZE EXECUTION SERVICES
   |
VERIFY PERSISTENT STORAGE
   |
READY
```

## 11.2 Bootstrap algorithm

```text
FUNCTION BOOTSTRAP_SYSTEM(configuration):

    VERIFY configuration.signature
    VERIFY approved_protocol_version
    VERIFY validator_membership
    VERIFY policy_hash
    VERIFY cryptographic_keys
    VERIFY storage_integrity

    IF any critical check fails:
        ENTER SAFE_MODE
        RECORD_BOOTSTRAP_FAILURE
        RETURN SUSPEND

    provision = REQUEST_AUTHORIZED_RESOURCES()

    VERIFY provision.attestations
    ENFORCE resource ceilings
    INITIALIZE isolated execution environment

    VERIFY environment identity
    VERIFY storage availability
    VERIFY audit pipeline

    IF all checks pass:
        RETURN READY

    RETURN SUSPEND
```

## 11.3 Bootstrap safeguards

- Maximum resource ceilings.
- Maximum initialization retries.
- Signed configuration.
- Trusted membership registry.
- Explicit provisioning authorization.
- Isolated execution environments.
- No unrestricted recursive provisioning.
- Fail-closed behavior for critical identity or integrity failures.

Self-bootstrapping does not mean the system can grant itself unlimited authority.

