* 7 validators, tolerating up to 2 Byzantine validators under the selected BFT assumptions.

* 3 execution branches: primary, parallel, fallback.

* 6 parallel workers.

* Signed task-binding manifests.

* One PPSA checkpoint repository.

* Fault injection for equivocation, replay, corrupted storage, and interrupted execution.

* Automated checks for conflicting commits and unauthorized execution.

The next engineering step is to turn this specification into an executable reference model and test harness. 
